{"title":"Nej til pesticider i grundvandet","description":"","products":[{"product_id":"waterpitcher","title":"Postevand Water Pitcher","description":"\u003cdiv data-paragraph=\"true\"\u003e\n\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Postevand water pitcher is the first in a series of water carriers we will introduce. Created in collaboration with glass designer Marie Breyen, it is the first physical manifestation in a new collection of objects exploring the essence of water. The pitcher carries the imprint of nature: its form is blown into the bark of a Scots pine, leaving the tree’s texture as a hidden structure within the glass. Technically, the pitcher is crafted from two layers of glass—the first shaped as a bottle, followed by an additional layer blown into the bark mold. The neck is drawn and opened with glass shears.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMarie Breyen is a trained glassblower, graduating from The National School of Glass (Riksglasskolan) in Sweden (2016–2019), where she received a classical, technical education. She later earned a degree from The Royal Danish Academy, Bornholm, in Crafts with a focus on glass and ceramics (2019–2023).\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnly eight unique pitchers have been created, each distinct in its own way.\u003c\/p\u003e\n\u003c\/div\u003e","brand":"Postevand","offers":[{"title":"Onesize","offer_id":31003123712066,"sku":"","price":1500.0,"currency_code":"DKK","in_stock":false}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/1721\/2643\/files\/pitcher-main.png?v=1784120513"}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/1721\/2643\/collections\/IMG_20190912_0141s.jpg?v=1572000711","url":"https:\/\/postevand.com\/collections\/nej-til-pesticider-i-grundvandet.oembed","provider":"Postevand","version":"1.0","type":"link"}